            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\n> 4\\. Type `<tag>text</tag>` in insert mode, type `srt` in normal mode, try to write a tag name, output is cut off after the first character.\n\nReplacing a surrounding requires two identifiers:\n- First is an \"input\" identifier used to detect which surrounding is replaced. That is `t` for tag in this case.\n- Second is an \"output\" identifier used to determine *with which* surrounding to replace. The `t` is also for \"tag\" here.\n\nSo this should be the following key presses: `sr` (surround replace) -> `t` (tag) -> `t` (with tag) -> `new-tag` (enter name of the new tag) -> `<CR>` (confirm new name).",
